1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,856
这是我们原型里的一个 bug
Here is a bug in our prototype.

2
00:00:02,176 --> 00:00:06,429
一个学生拿到了耳鼻喉专科的转诊
A student has a referral to an ear, nose and throat specialist,

3
00:00:06,429 --> 00:00:08,725
有效期到 1 月 22 日
valid until January twenty-second.

4
00:00:09,045 --> 00:00:14,421
家长打开预约页面，一直开着，过了有效期才点提交
Their parent opens the booking page, leaves it open past that moment, and presses submit.

5
00:00:14,741 --> 00:00:19,382
按 agent 对代码的分析，过期的转诊照样被关联上
By the agent's reading of the code, the expired referral is attached anyway,

6
00:00:19,382 --> 00:00:23,168
进度页显示已预约专科，而不是已过期
and the tracker shows the specialist as booked, never expired.

7
00:00:23,417 --> 00:00:28,857
现有的 245 个测试全部通过；没有一个是在过期之后预约的
All 245 existing tests passed; none of them books after the expiry.

8
00:00:29,177 --> 00:00:33,529
代码里甚至有一行注释，说过期的转诊保持不变
The code even carries a comment saying expired referrals are left alone.

9
00:00:33,849 --> 00:00:35,449
没有人注意到
No person had noticed.

10
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:38,305
周五下午，一个 agent 报告了它
On Friday afternoon an agent reported it,

11
00:00:38,305 --> 00:00:42,169
它在一个很小的世界里，试遍了几种操作的所有顺序
after trying every order of a few actions in a small world.

12
00:00:42,489 --> 00:00:47,459
这一集讲的是：在有人看之前，agent 怎么证明一个改动是对的
This episode is about how an agent can prove a change is right before anyone looks.

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,981
App 数据的每一次变化，都要经过同一个函数，叫 reducer
Every change to the app's data goes through one function, called the reducer.

14
00:00:53,301 --> 00:00:56,325
它拿到当前状态和一个操作
It takes the current state and a single action,

15
00:00:56,325 --> 00:01:01,600
比如预约、确认、改期、取消、完成，然后返回下一个状态
such as book, confirm, reschedule, cancel or complete, and returns the next state.

16
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:04,786
预约页面在画出来的时候检查转诊
The booking page checks the referral when it draws,

17
00:01:04,786 --> 00:01:07,147
但预约要过一会儿才到 reducer
but the booking reaches the reducer later.

18
00:01:07,467 --> 00:01:11,221
所以事件的顺序很重要，时间流逝也是一个事件
So the order of events matters, and time passing is an event too.

19
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:13,728
测试走的是某人选好的一条路
A test follows a path someone chose.

20
00:01:14,048 --> 00:01:19,253
bug 藏在一条没人选的路上：先是时间过去，然后预约成功
The bug lives on a path nobody chose: first time passes, then the booking goes through.

21
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,932
测试检查的是有人想到的情况
A test checks the cases someone thought of.

22
00:01:22,252 --> 00:01:24,151
那没人想到的情况，谁来检查？
What checks the ones nobody thought of?

23
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,767
换个办法，搭一个很小的世界
Build a small world instead:

24
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:34,375
两张转诊、三个专科时段，还有一个只有两个时刻的时钟
two referrals, three specialist slots, and a clock with just two moments,

25
00:01:34,375 --> 00:01:38,667
一个是转诊刚开出来，一个是过期后一小时
right after the referrals are written and an hour after they expire.

26
00:01:38,987 --> 00:01:42,080
从起点出发，第一步有 13 种可能
From the starting state there are thirteen possible moves.

27
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,241
每一种都走一遍，再从每个结果出发走下一步
Make each one, then every move from each result,

28
00:01:45,241 --> 00:01:48,437
一层一层往下，遇到见过的状态就合并
layer by layer, merging any state you've already seen.

29
00:01:48,757 --> 00:01:53,628
在这个世界里一共是 13,898 个状态，大约一秒走完
In this world that is 13,898 states, reached in about a second,

30
00:01:53,628 --> 00:01:58,421
而且每一个都来自真正的 reducer，不是复制品
and every one of them comes from the real reducer, not a copy.

31
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:01,011
每个状态检查四条规则
Four rules are checked at every state

32
00:02:01,011 --> 00:02:04,623
每一步再检查第五条，全部用大白话写成
and a fifth on every step, all written in plain language,

33
00:02:04,623 --> 00:02:11,275
比如一张转诊最多对应一个有效预约，过期的转诊不会被新关联上
such as one referral backs at most one live appointment, and an expired referral is never newly attached.

34
00:02:11,595 --> 00:02:15,571
因为搜索是一层一层进行的，遇到的第一条被打破的规则
Because the search goes layer by layer, the first broken rule it meets comes

35
00:02:15,571 --> 00:02:17,611
给出的就是打破它的最短步骤
with the shortest story that breaks it.

36
00:02:17,931 --> 00:02:21,429
这里是两步：时间过去，然后用这张转诊预约
Here, two steps: time passes, then book with that referral.

37
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,338
它为什么没被发现？
Why did it slip through?

38
00:02:24,388 --> 00:02:27,119
预约只看转诊里存着的状态
Booking looks only at the referral's stored status.

39
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:31,108
已过期这个状态从来不存，只是显示的时候算出来
Expired is never stored; it is only worked out for the screen.

40
00:02:31,428 --> 00:02:34,372
而且页面在画出来时检查，不是在你提交时检查
And the page checks when it draws, not when you submit.

41
00:02:34,692 --> 00:02:37,103
agent 没有改产品代码
The agent did not change the product code.

42
00:02:37,423 --> 00:02:41,870
它把这个 bug 记成已知发现，把修法留给人来定
It recorded the bug as a known finding and left the fix to a person:

43
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:46,383
在 reducer 里比较有效期，或者提交时再检查一次
compare the expiry date inside the reducer, or check again on submit.

44
00:02:46,617 --> 00:02:49,348
规则没有为了让检查通过而放宽
The rule was not loosened to make the check pass.

45
00:02:49,668 --> 00:02:52,271
而且检查会在两种情况下失败
And the check is built to fail in two ways:

46
00:02:52,271 --> 00:02:56,025
任何一条新规则被打破，或者这个已知的 bug 消失了
if any new rule breaks, and if this known bug ever disappears.

47
00:02:56,345 --> 00:02:59,876
第二种失败会提醒修好它的人把这条记录删掉
That second failure reminds whoever fixes it to delete the note,

48
00:02:59,876 --> 00:03:02,745
免得这个 bug 哪天回来时被它挡住
so the note can never hide the bug if it comes back.

49
00:03:04,083 --> 00:03:06,814
agent 为什么要故意把自己的代码改坏？
Why would an agent break its own code on purpose?

50
00:03:10,683 --> 00:03:13,435
因为一个你从没见过它失败的检查，什么也证明不了
Because a check you have never seen fail proves nothing.

51
00:03:13,755 --> 00:03:15,376
也许它根本就不会失败
Maybe it can't fail at all.

52
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:18,982
所以 agent 故意把 reducer 改坏了五次
So the agent broke the reducer five times on purpose,

53
00:03:18,982 --> 00:03:22,267
五种不同的改法，每次改完都跑一遍检查
in five different ways, and ran the check after each.

54
00:03:22,587 --> 00:03:26,528
五次都被抓到了，每次的复现都不超过两步
All five were caught, each with a story of two steps or fewer,

55
00:03:26,528 --> 00:03:28,688
改坏的地方随后都改了回去
and each breakage was then undone.

56
00:03:29,008 --> 00:03:33,889
这是测试人员所说的变异测试的手工版
It is a hand-made version of what testers call mutation testing;

57
00:03:33,889 --> 00:03:36,710
这方面的经典论文发表于 1978 年
the classic paper on it is from 1978.

58
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:39,927
这个思路由来已久，也很严肃
The idea is old and serious.

59
00:03:40,247 --> 00:03:45,087
2015 年，Amazon 介绍了他们用这种方法检查设计
In 2015 Amazon described checking its designs this way,

60
00:03:45,087 --> 00:03:49,399
用的是 TLA plus，一种由 Leslie Lamport 创造的语言
using TLA+, a language created by Leslie Lamport.

61
00:03:49,719 --> 00:03:52,881
在一个数据库服务里，它找到了一个会丢数据的 bug
In one database service it found a data-loss bug

62
00:03:52,881 --> 00:03:56,044
最短的复现有 35 步
whose shortest story was thirty-five steps long,

63
00:03:56,044 --> 00:04:00,194
而这个 bug 之前通过了设计审查、代码审查和测试
a bug that had passed design reviews, code reviews and testing.

64
00:04:00,514 --> 00:04:04,499
我们的相比之下很小，一秒钟的检查里只有两步
Ours is tiny by comparison, two steps in a one-second check,

65
00:04:04,499 --> 00:04:09,879
但做的是同一件事：让机器去走人永远不会去试的每一种顺序
but it is the same move: let a machine walk every order a person would never try.

66
00:04:11,217 --> 00:04:14,716
第二个工具直接操作 App，就像家长那样
The second tool drives the app itself, the way a parent would.

67
00:04:15,036 --> 00:04:16,847
agent 从一份保存好的演示状态出发
From a saved demo state,

68
00:04:16,847 --> 00:04:20,177
启动自己的一份 App 和自己的浏览器
the agent starts its own copy of the app and its own browser.

69
00:04:20,497 --> 00:04:24,659
然后它一步步点：打开转诊，选一家网络内的诊所
Then it clicks through: open the referral, choose an in-network clinic,

70
00:04:24,659 --> 00:04:27,942
选时间，提交，等待待确认，打开进度页
pick a time, submit, wait for pending, open the tracker.

71
00:04:28,262 --> 00:04:31,643
它按角色和无障碍名称来找每一个控件
It finds each control by its role and accessible name,

72
00:04:31,643 --> 00:04:33,897
也就是读屏软件念出来的那个名字
the label a screen reader announces,

73
00:04:33,897 --> 00:04:36,966
并且每一步之后都等页面安静下来
and waits for the page to settle after each step.

74
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:41,431
做对了，要两件事同时成立：屏幕上显示专科已预约
Right means two things at once: the screen says the specialist is booked,

75
00:04:41,431 --> 00:04:45,605
保存的数据里转诊也指向了这个新预约
and the saved data says the referral now points to that new appointment.

76
00:04:45,925 --> 00:04:51,941
每次运行都必须留下证据：截图、保存的状态，以及没有浏览器报错
Each run is required to keep evidence: screenshots, the saved state, and no browser errors.

77
00:04:52,261 --> 00:04:55,632
某一步失败时，它会告诉你它能看到哪些按钮
When a step fails, it says which buttons it could see instead.

78
00:04:55,952 --> 00:04:58,982
结束时，它只关掉自己启动的东西
And when it's done, it shuts down only what it started.

79
00:05:00,317 --> 00:05:05,004
这两个工具都来自一个公开插件 pstack 里的两个 skill
Both tools came from trying two skills in a public plugin called pstack,

80
00:05:05,004 --> 00:05:09,106
是周五下午试用时做的，两次提交相隔 27 分钟
on Friday afternoon, in two commits twenty-seven minutes apart.

81
00:05:09,426 --> 00:05:13,579
Anthropic 自己给 Claude Code 的建议说得很直白
Anthropic's own advice for Claude Code says the same thing plainly:

82
00:05:13,579 --> 00:05:17,298
给 agent 一个能跑的检查，否则你自己就成了测试
give the agent a check to run, or you become the test suite.

83
00:05:17,534 --> 00:05:21,448
等你来做的事：选定过期转诊的修法
What waits for you: choosing the fix for the expired referral,

84
00:05:21,448 --> 00:05:24,669
以及在你自己的电脑上试一下这个操作 App 的工具
and trying the app-driving tool on your own laptop;

85
00:05:24,669 --> 00:05:26,942
目前它只在云端跑过
so far it has only run in the cloud.

86
00:05:27,262 --> 00:05:29,182
这个 PR 也还是草稿
And the pull request is still a draft.

87
00:05:29,502 --> 00:05:33,363
上一集问的是：层层叠加的检查，能不能代替人工审查
The last episode asked whether layers can stand in for a human review.

88
00:05:33,683 --> 00:05:36,845
这里又多了两层：一个试遍所有顺序的检查
Here are two more: a check that tries every order,

89
00:05:36,845 --> 00:05:39,123
和一个真的去用 App 的 agent
and an agent that uses the real app.

90
00:05:40,467 --> 00:05:44,830
所以：一个工具在小世界里走遍所有操作顺序
So: one tool walks every order of actions in a small world and hands back

91
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:47,102
交回打破规则的最短复现
the shortest story that breaks a rule.

92
00:05:47,422 --> 00:05:51,134
另一个工具像家长一样真的去用 App，并留下证据
The other uses the real app like a parent and keeps the evidence.

93
00:05:51,454 --> 00:05:54,327
第一个是靠故意改坏来检验的
The first was checked by breaking it on purpose;

94
00:05:54,327 --> 00:05:57,022
第二个是靠把每个流程从头到尾跑一遍
the second, by running every flow end to end.

95
00:05:57,267 --> 00:05:58,646
三个问题
Three questions.

96
00:05:58,696 --> 00:06:02,110
穷举检查试了哪些普通测试不会试的东西？
What does the exhaustive check try that an ordinary test doesn't?

97
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:04,328
为什么要故意把自己的代码改坏？
Why break your own code on purpose?

98
00:06:04,648 --> 00:06:07,230
为什么 bug 修好以后，检查反而会失败？
And why does the check fail when the bug gets fixed?

99
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:16,606
下一集：在写任何后端代码之前，后端怎么选？
Next: before any backend code is written, how do you choose the backend?
